<%#
  Which project a monitor belongs to. The move CONTROL is gone with the rest of
  the manual path (v1-scope §3.3) — it was `manual?`-only, and §11 accepts the
  capability loss for the frozen backfilled population rather than keep a second
  writer alive for it.

  The heading and the "In <project>" link stay: this is the only place the detail
  page names the monitor's project.

  The retained note is branched on `source` rather than shown to everyone (§11).
  "Managed by the gem — re-point its API key" is true of a synced monitor and
  false in both halves for a backfilled `manual-<id>` row: no gem manages it and
  no API key syncs it. Such a row gets no note here — the config panel above
  already tells it its settings are frozen and what the remedy is.

  Locals: monitor.
%>
<div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-6 shadow-sm" data-testid="monitor-project-card">
  <h2 class="text-[13px] font-semibold text-secondary mb-3">Project</h2>
  <p class="text-[13px] text-muted">
    In <%= link_to monitor.project.name, project_path(monitor.project), class: "font-medium text-ink hover:text-brand" %>.
  </p>

  <% if monitor.from_gem? %>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[12px] text-muted" data-testid="move-gem-note">
      Managed by the gem — re-point its API key to move it to another project.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
